// GENERATED FILE — do not hand-edit.
// PT Mono TTF (Latin + Cyrillic subsets merged), base64-encoded for
// embedding into client-generated PDFs via jsPDF's addFileToVFS/addFont.
// jsPDF's built-in fonts (helvetica/courier/times) have no Cyrillic glyphs,
// so Ukrainian receipt text needs a real embedded font. PT Mono was chosen
// (over the site's own Comfortaa) specifically for the receipt PDF because
// it is a fixed-width font with full Cyrillic support — closer to the
// monospace "Courier New"/thermal-printer look the receipt is meant to
// mimic (see utils/receiptPdf.ts) than a rounded proportional font. It ships
// only a Regular (400) cut, no bold — receiptPdf.ts fakes bold by
// fill-then-stroking the text instead of switching font weight.
//
// @fontsource ships each weight split into several woff2 files by Unicode
// range (latin, latin-ext, cyrillic, cyrillic-ext — browsers only download
// the range a page actually needs via unicode-range in the generated
// @font-face rules). A single one of those files is NOT a usable standalone
// font on its own, so this merges the "latin" + "cyrillic" woff2 subsets
// back into one font (315 codepoints — full Latin/digits/punctuation plus
// the complete Ukrainian/Russian alphabet incl. Ґ/ґ and №), converted from
// woff2 to ttf with fonttools (jsPDF needs a raw TTF, not woff2) via:
//   fontTools.merge latin-400.ttf cyr-400.ttf --output-file=merged-400.ttf

export const PT_MONO_BASE64 = "";
